<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>General on University of Michigan Fencing Club</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/categories/general/</link><description>Recent content in General on University of Michigan Fencing Club</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>(c) 2025 University of Michigan Fencing Club</copyright><lastBuildDate>Tue, 28 Jun 2016 14:49:10 -0700</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.um-fencing.com/categories/general/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Donate</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/donate/</link><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jun 2016 14:49:10 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/donate/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The University of Michigan Fencing Club is excited about the upcoming season.&#10;We are not only eager to defend our title as the USACFC national champions, but we want everyone on campus to have the opportunity to join our club, learn how to fence, and take fencing with them for the rest of their lives.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;One of our top priorities is investing in the future to create a growing and sustainable organization.&#10;With your help we can continue to compete at the highest level while offering the beginning of a lifelong experience for UofM students.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>About Fencing</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/about_fencing/</link><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jun 2016 14:07:29 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/about_fencing/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The sport of fencing has three weapons: foil, epee and saber.&#10;The object of a fencing bout (what an individual &amp;ldquo;game&amp;rdquo; is called) is to land a specified number of touches on your opponent before he/she scores that number on you.&#10;Each bout is officiated by a referee called a director.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="electric-scoring"&gt;Electric Scoring&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;All official tournaments are conducted using electric scoring systems.&#10;The fencers connect themselves, their blades, and their metal jackets (lames) to a retractable cord (reel), which plugs in to a scoring machine (pictured left).&#10;The machine shows a light for each fencer who successfully scores a touch on his or her opponent.&#10;The director then describes the action and awards points based on right-of-way.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Contact</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/contact/</link><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jun 2016 15:09:24 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/contact/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;d love to hear from you! If you have a question, you can ask any of our officers at practice or contact us electronically.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="container-fluid"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="row"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="col-md-6"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="alert alert-info" role="alert"&gt;&#13;&#10; Have general inquiry questions?&#10;Email us at &lt;a href="mailto:fencingofficers@umich.edu"&gt;fencingofficers@umich.edu&lt;/a&gt;.&#10;We can help in person, too. Stop by during any practice and we&amp;rsquo;ll take care of you.&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="col-md-6"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="alert alert-info" role="alert"&gt;&#13;&#10; Want to anonymously give feedback, ask a question, raise a concern, etc.?&#10;Please use our &lt;a href="https://forms.gle/jgLxrP3zrSTAueLGA"&gt;suggestions box&lt;/a&gt;.&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="officers"&gt;Officers&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Position&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Email Address&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Contact About&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/